NNAAMMEE
       pgmabel - create cross section using Abel Integration for Deconvolution


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppggmmaabbeell [--hheellpp] [--aaxxiiss _a_x_i_s] [--ffaaccttoorr _f_a_c_t_o_r] [--ppiixxssiizzee _p_i_x_s_i_z_e] [--lleefftt
       | --rriigghhtt] [--vveerrbboossee] [_f_i_l_e_s_p_e_c]


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppggmmaabbeell reads as input a PGM image, which it assumes to be an image  of
       a  rotational symmetric transparent object.  The image must have a ver‐
       tical symmetry axis.  ppggmmaabbeell produces as output an image of  a  cross-
       section of the image.

       ppggmmaabbeell does the calculation by performing the Abel Integration for De‐
       convolution of an axial-symmetrical image by solving the system of lin‐
       ear equations.

       After  integration,  ppggmmaabbeell weights all gray-values of one side by the
       surface area of the calculated ring in square pixels divided by  4*_f_a_c_‐
       _t_o_r  multiplied  by the size of one pixel (_p_i_x_s_i_z_e).  With the --vveerrbboossee
       option, ppggmmaabbeell prints the weighting factors.

       Where the calculation generates a negative result, the output is black.

       The computation is unstable against periodic structures with size 2  in
       the vertical direction.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ),  ppggmmaabbeell  recognizes  the
       following command line options:

       You can abbreviate any option to its shortest unique prefix.




       --hheellpp  Prints a help message.


       --aaxxiiss _a_x_i_s
              Position of the axis of symmetry in the image in pixels from the
              left edge of the image.  Default is the center of the image.


       --ffaaccttoorr _f_a_c_t_o_r
              User defined factor for enhancement of the output.  Use a _f_a_c_t_o_r
              less than 1 for decreasing gary values.  Default is 1.0.


       --ppiixxssiizzee _p_i_x_s_i_z_e
              The  size  of  a  pixel for getting scale invariant.  Default is
              0.1.


       --lleefftt  Calculate only the left side of the image.  You  cannot  specify
              both lleefftt and rriigghhtt.


       --rriigghhtt Analogous to --lleefftt.


       --vveerrbboossee
              print information about the calculation.




EEXXAAMMPPLLEE
       Rotate  a  PGM  image to get an image with a vertical axis of symmetry,
       then calculate the cross section:

           pnmrotate 90 file.pgm | pgmabel -axis 140 >cross_section.pgm



